{"id": "EUVD-2026-101928", "enisaUuid": "d2e6fda6-c767-34b5-afa3-ddaec35abbbf", "description": "In Eclipse Vert.x versions [5.0.0,5.0.12] or [5.1.0,5.1.9] or [5.2.0, 5.2.0], the HTTP proxy provides a body transformer interceptor that relies on a max buffered bytes limit to ensure a bounded buffer for each request. This can be used to force a server to indefinitely allocate heap. This vulnerability requires to use an intercepting body transformer.\n\n\n\nThe impacted component is io.vertx:vertx-http-proxy.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T07:24:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T14:35:42", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/eclipse-vertx/vertx-http-proxy/security/advisories/GHSA-mjwh-5qfp-hjgc", "https://gitlab.eclipse.org/security/cve-assignment/-/work_items/351"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-102475", "GHSA-67g8-jf88-4xjq"], "assigner": "eclipse", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "18ba41d6-3a30-3e6a-933a-b20bbc5f2dc2", "product": {"name": "Eclipse Vert.x", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "5.0.0 \u22645.0.12"}, {"id": "447e2d22-571e-3c36-9dd5-f2f63f9f6f3e", "product": {"name": "Eclipse Vert.x", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "5.1.0 \u22645.1.9"}, {"id": "6eb7ff32-136a-3f02-be60-b5e110defc89", "product": {"name": "Eclipse Vert.x", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "5.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "04bdfb13-e8f0-351d-b0b3-843e7cbf5980", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}